<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<gpx version="1.1" creator="Good Shit" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1"><trk><name>Alden / Norskehesten — Aldenvågen, Instenova and Ystenova crest return [planning only — not navigation-grade]</name><desc>From Aldenvågen on Alden in Norway’s Vestland region, take the signed farm approach and steep path to the plateau. Visit Instenova, return to the junction, then follow the western path to Ystenova for sea and island views before retracing your steps. Allow roughly 3.5 hours for 5.9 km and about 480 m of climbing; these are approximate planning figures. Mountain paths are unmarked. Avoid strong wind, rain, snow and ice, stay back from cliff edges and respect farm boundaries. Confirm outward and return boats and current landing terms; closures or unsafe sections can make the whole outing unavailable.

Route geometry: © Kartverket — https://www.kartverket.no/; N50 Kartdata Samferdsel, CC BY 4.0 — https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/. Dataset: https://www.geonorge.no/geonetwork/srv/api/records/ea192681-d039-42ec-b1bc-f3ce04c189ac/formatters/xml. Source: https://nedlasting.geonorge.no/geonorge/Basisdata/N50Kartdata/GML/Basisdata_4645_Askvoll_25832_N50Kartdata_GML.zip. Changes: four whole original road and footpath features, in their literal source order, transformed from ETRS89 / UTM zone 32N (EPSG:25832) to WGS84 longitude/latitude (EPSG:4326), with the eastern and western crest legs retraced to the same landing. Only duplicate shared junction vertices removed; canonical display simplified using original transformed source vertices. No synthetic connectors, summit-point snaps, cross-source geometry or elevations. Planning only; not navigation-grade.

